904 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186535570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535904 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bdcdafbc-2a00-5bc3-a5dd-993258a4e62f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535905 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186535760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535905 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535905 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535905 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186535760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535905 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c0cddfae-ecf5-50fd-9bfc-04c2102bb55f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535919 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186535546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535919 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186535547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535919 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186535653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535919 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186535801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535919 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535919 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535919 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186535546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535919 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f1dc9399-c403-56eb-8f48-08331960ca43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535950 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186535905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535950 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335062" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535950 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535950 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535950 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5cb555db-6a59-509d-947e-27c4f1a2a7e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535950 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535981 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186535834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535981 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186535904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535981 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186535919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535981 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335403" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535981 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535981 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by  \n{{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535981 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ace7005c-d6c8-5219-91cc-32f47feb4972" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535981 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Differentiating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ and applying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-At})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating and using the product rule}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\ny(0)={e}^{-A\\cdot 0}x(0)=Ix(0)=x(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t=0.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,ds\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L6}$ by ${e}^{At}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}y(t) & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{e}^{At}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{At}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536011 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186536036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536011 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1c1ad14e-74e6-51e6-a61f-0245fb4cfb09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536011 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186308719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536026 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186536050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536026 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6904603d-53fd-531b-aed9-20fdeb45db7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536026 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186311584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536029 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7a5de0ff-7990-5b8c-9f62-a36d2977e2f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536029 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186370330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536036 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186536026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536036 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "98ff146f-1e74-5987-92d5-7e14960c7748" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536036 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186535950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536050 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186536029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536050 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f824fb6b-0584-52aa-83b5-662d7f07a788" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536050 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186535981 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
